<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-curator-housekeeping</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 3500 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' __APP_DIR__/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" "http://localhost:3000/api/cron/curator?housekeeping=1"</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    23:10 nightly — fold duplicate staged proposals.

    ⚠ A SEPARATE AGENT FROM THE CURATOR BECAUSE OF THE MODEL, NOT THE LOGIC.
    `dedupePendingSessions` makes one grouping call per batch with up to a
    45-minute budget; the curator makes none and runs in seconds. Putting them
    on one schedule would mean either the fold ran in front of the morning
    brief or the curation waited until midnight. Same route, different hour.

    23:10 is clear of everything: risk-scores 01:00, contacts-sync 02:45,
    drive-sync 03:15, drive-publish 03:45, lead-sweep 04:30, imessage-sweep
    04:40, chase 05:30, curator 06:20, brief 06:30, text 06:45, note 06:50,
    digest 07:00, and the hourly drive-watch / meet-import pairs which stop at
    12:20 and 16:20.

    ⚠ 212 staged proposals as of 2026-10-12, 100 of them over thirty days old —
    and the oldest are LIVE deals already on the books (IAN Acquisition,
    Fort Polk, Myton islanded grid), which is why there is no retire-by-age
    rule anywhere in this feature. What makes a staged proposal disposable is
    that its deal already exists, which is this pass's question.
  -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>23</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>10</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-curator-housekeeping.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/cron-curator-housekeeping.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
